import Mathlib

/-!
# The Fourier Analysis of Collatz: Spectral Gaps in the 3n+1 Map

This file studies the **linear (affine) part of the Collatz / Syracuse step**,
`x ↦ 3x + 1`, as a dynamical system on the finite cyclic group `ℤ/N` (`ZMod N`),
through the lens of harmonic analysis on finite abelian groups.

The Collatz map proper is `n ↦ n/2` (n even), `n ↦ 3n+1` (n odd).  Its arithmetic
difficulty lives in the *coupling* of the affine branch `3n+1` with the `2`-adic
contraction `n/2`.  Here we isolate the affine branch and analyse the **Koopman
(composition) operator** `U f = f ∘ A`, `A x = 3x+1`, on `ℂ`-valued functions on
`ℤ/N`, using the additive characters of `ℤ/N` as a Fourier basis.

## Main results

* `CollatzFourier.affine_bijective` — `A` is a bijection of `ℤ/N` exactly when `3`
  is a unit mod `N` (i.e. `gcd(3,N)=1`).
* `CollatzFourier.koopman_addChar` — the Koopman operator sends each additive
  character `ψ` to a *phase times another character*:
  `U ψ (x) = ψ(1) · ψ(3x)`.  Thus on the Fourier side `U` acts by the frequency
  map `m ↦ 3m` together with a unit-modulus phase.
* `CollatzFourier.koopman_iterate_addChar` — closed form for the `k`-fold iterate:
  `Uᵏ ψ (x) = ψ(∑_{j<k} 3ʲ) · ψ(3ᵏ x)`.
* `CollatzFourier.koopman_eigen_of_order` / `no_spectral_gap` — if `3^L = 1` in
  `ℤ/N` (e.g. `L = ord_N(3)`), then **every additive character is an eigenvector**
  of `Uᴸ` with a **unimodular eigenvalue** `c`, `‖c‖ = 1`.
* `CollatzFourier.koopman_l2_isometry` — when `A` is a bijection, `U` is an
  `L²`-isometry: `∑_x ‖U f (x)‖² = ∑_x ‖f(x)‖²`.

## Headline finding (the "spectral gap")

The affine `3n+1` map on any finite cyclic group has **NO spectral gap**: its
Koopman operator is (when `gcd(3,N)=1`) a unitary phase-permutation of the
character basis, so its entire spectrum lies on the unit circle and `Uᴸ` has all
eigenvalues of modulus `1`.  Equivalently, the affine branch is *measure
preserving and non-mixing*.  This is a precise obstruction: any spectral/mixing
route to Collatz cannot come from the affine branch alone — the contraction must
be supplied entirely by the `2`-adic `n/2` branch.  The relevant "frequency" time
scale is the multiplicative order `ord_N(3)`.

-- !-- Lab Notes -- !--
-- Hypothesis H1: "the 3n+1 map mixes / has a spectral gap on ℤ/N."
--   Outcome: FALSE on the affine branch. The Koopman operator merely permutes
--   characters m ↦ 3m up to phase (koopman_addChar), so its spectrum is on the
--   unit circle. Reframed as the *positive* theorem no_spectral_gap.
-- Hypothesis H2: "Iterating U scrambles a character into a genuine superposition."
--   Outcome: FALSE. koopman_iterate_addChar shows Uᵏψ stays a single character
--   times a phase; the geometric sum ∑ 3ʲ is the only bookkeeping needed.
-- Insight I1: The natural time scale is ord_N(3): after L = ord_N(3) steps the
--   frequency returns to itself and U^L acts as a scalar (koopman_eigen_of_order).
-- Insight I2: Bijectivity of A ⇔ gcd(3,N)=1 is the exact condition for U to be
